This name of the author of this book is Viktor Frankl(if I am right). This is about the holocaust and concentration camps in which the prisoners of the war were kept during the second world war. The author was one of the survivor of the holocaust. He described the environment and situation of a concentration camp, he told a bit about his family, perspective of different people towards the circumstances. 

During the world II when the people were taken to the concentration camp, author was one of them. The author had a chance to leave the country before the situation actually happened but he refused to leave his parent there and did not go and eventually ended up in the concentration camp. His was not the only one from his family to end up in a concentration camp, his father, mother, brother, and his pregnant wife were also taken to different camps. But in the end from his family he was the alone survivor. In those camps weather was extremely cold and all those prisoners did not have adequate clothing. They were given death punishment for small mistakes by shutting them to gas chambers, they made work in very poor conditions where most of them caught disease, many people's feet got injured because of the poor boots and the cold, many died of the disease and many by taking to the gas chambers, they had no hope of getting release or having any future.

Every person was living in the consistent fear of death, no one was sure for single day that he would be able to see the tomorrow. But the author notice that despite these circumstances which could be the worst of the circumstances one could be put in in his whole life, despite of these people were ready to give their bread to other people who need it more, people were ready to take risk to save the lives of other people, people were able to crack jokes and make other people laugh even in those intensely bad conditions. He concluded that something was there which was serving as life driven for them and those were there values, there values to be kind to other human beings there values be compassionate, to be empathetic. 

The author said between the stimuli and the reaction there is time in which we can decide whether to react to it or not if react then how to, and in that time our growth lies as a human being. The author said that a man can not choose his circumstances but he can always choose how to react to them. 

The question which is also the very title of book as well, 'What is the meaning of life?', the author did not answer the question rather he changed the question altogether. He says that we must stop asking for the meaning of life because it is us who are being question by the life itself. The only ways to live is to live according to your values and abandon those deeds which do not serve to your values.

The one important factor that why the author was able to observe those people in concentration camp so accurately was he was a professional psychiatrist. And at the end of the book he also talks about the therapy technique he developed after returning from the camp which he named as 'Logotherapy'.

One of my personal reason to recommend this book to anyone is that one, it is relatively short so if the person is not in reading he can also manage to finish it and second there are people who at a point in their life ask this question are the related question that 'What is the meaning of life?'.   